{"version":1,"entries":{"Narrator: We live in families. People in families help each other. They love each other, too. Not all families are the same. There are many kinds of families. Meet Seb. He's seven years old. Seb's family is big. He lives with his mother, father, three brothers, and two sisters.\n\nSeb's family: We work together.\n\nNarrator: This is Mandy. She's eight years old. She has one brother. They live with their grandmother and grandfather.\n\nMandy's family: We go places together.\n\nNarrator: This is Kim. She's six years old. Her family is small. She lives with her mother.\n\nKim's family: We spend time together.\n\nNarrator: Which family is like your family? Friends are also important. Friends have fun together, and they help each other, too. Seb, Mandy, and Kim are good friends. They go to school together. They play together every day.\n\nFriends: We share things.\n\nNarrator: Who are your good friends?":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9c8525c79a1c178a1b6c.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5962b8b207f6ef6cbdc6.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Seb's family"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/06229516016a9d097280.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4de25ab7320112607aa5.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Mandy's family"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/32f48aaff15125def983.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/efc18ddc39e01eb3b806.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Kim's family"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ebe620dfe05e9f7fd7b0.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f21a68c25314f031dd6e.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Friends"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/17266afa59a9a06e93df.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Narrator"}],"Narrator: Elliot is a sad and lonely little elephant. He can't find his family. He walks and walks. He sees some tortoises.\n\nTuti: Hello, I'm Tuti. Who are you?\n\nElliot: I'm Elliot. I can't find my family.\n\nTuti: I can help. Let's go.\n\nNarrator: They walk and walk. They see some zebras.\n\nTuti: Is that your family?\n\nElliot: No! Those are zebras. I'm not a zebra. I'm an elephant.\n\nNarrator: The zebras see Elliot and Tuti. The zebras are scared and they run away. Tuti is Elliot's new friend. They eat together and they play together. Then they walk and walk again. They see some lions.\n\nTuti: Is that your family?\n\nElliot: No! Those are lions. I'm not a lion. I'm an elephant.\n\nNarrator: The lions see Elliot and Tuti. Elliot and Tuti are scared and they run away. It's nighttime. They sleep side by side. The next day, they walk and walk again. They see some elephants.\n\nTuti: Is that your family?\n\nElliot: Yes! Those are elephants. I'm an elephant. Thank you, Tuti. You're my best friend.\n\nNarrator: Now Elliot has a family and a friend.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4e0f59a29d78a3d9dcb7.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/77e0889f808546480ab2.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Tuti"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1b375b2b5a038e7634cf.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Elliot"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3560dc67f07913e48588.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Tuti"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ab75e46eeb8f34f5bf19.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5496f0300149b315a618.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Tuti"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/d01fc937720b0c588c33.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Elliot"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/c9d77e4b93551ee3d419.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5496f0300149b315a618.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Tuti"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/cf8d2f47b87726886b37.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Elliot"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/096cf215146ae1f4f4bc.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5496f0300149b315a618.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Tuti"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a491efdeade2337b2eb4.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Elliot"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9c6098a05282df8d02bb.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Narrator"}],"Dian: This is a story about an orangutan called Anak, and how I teach her to live in the rainforest. My name is Dian. I take care of young orangutans at the Happy House Reserve. These young orangutans don't have families and can't live alone. The Happy House Reserve is in a rainforest. I teach the orangutans how to live in the rainforest. Anak is a baby. She lives at the reserve. I take care of her every day. I give her milk from a bottle. I teach Anak about the rainforest. We have fun together. Anak isn't sad or lonely. Anak is now four years old. She eats fruit, leaves, and flowers, and she can climb trees. She plays with her orangutan friends. But I am still Anak's special friend. Anak is eight years old now. She sleeps and eats at the reserve. I'm always happy to see her. She plays in the rainforest a lot. Sometimes she takes a nap there. I'm not with her in the rainforest. Anak is twelve years old now and she is very big. She lives and sleeps in the rainforest. I put out Anak's favorite foods, fruit and flowers, but she doesn't come. I miss Anak! Look! Who's this? It's Anak, and she has a baby! Anak and I are happy to see each other. I miss Anak every day, but I am happy. Anak can now live in the rainforest and teach her baby how to live there, too.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/60514a7d663dc674a602.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Dian"}],"Arnold: My name is Arnold. I have an apple tree. It keeps me busy all year. I watch small buds grow on my apple tree. They grow into apple blossoms. I watch honeybees collect nectar from the blossoms. I make a swing for my apple tree. I build a tree house in my apple tree. My apple tree shades me from the hot sun. I watch small apples begin to grow. I juggle some green apples for my tree friend. My apple tree now has big, red, tasty apples. I bring some leaves up to my tree house. I make a soft floor to lie on. I shake the branches. Red apples fall to the ground. I put them in a basket and take them home. My family and I make apple pies. In the winter, snow falls. It's quiet. The branches of my apple tree are bare. I hang strings of popcorn and berries on the branches. The birds eat them. I build a snowman. The snow melts. It's spring again.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/517699678e5335fafad4.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Arnold"}],"Narrator: Hans and his wife, Ann, and their daughter, Olga, walk to a town. They see a woman.\n\nHans: We're very hungry, says Hans. Do you have any food?\n\nWoman: No, says the woman. I'm hungry, too!\n\nNarrator: They see a man.\n\nOlga: Olga says, We're hungry. Do you have any food?\n\nMan: No, says the man. I'm hungry, too!\n\nNarrator: The family has a big pot. Hans puts water in it. Ann and Olga look for stones. They each find four stones and put them into the pot.\n\nWoman and her friend: What's that? ask the woman and her friend.\n\nHans: It's stone soup, says Hans. It's tasty. You can try some, but we don't have any potatoes. It's good with potatoes.\n\nWoman: I have five! says the woman.\n\nWoman's friend: I have seven, says her friend.\n\nNarrator: They put the potatoes into the pot.\n\nMan and his son: What's that? ask the man and his son.\n\nOlga: It's stone soup, says Olga. It's tasty. You can try some, but we don't have any sausages. It's good with sausages.\n\nMan: I have two, says the man.\n\nSon: I have three, says his son.\n\nNarrator: They put the sausages into the pot. Later, the people from the town smell the soup and come out to look.\n\nTownspeople: We have onions. We have carrots, they say, and put them into the pot.\n\nNarrator: Everyone eats some soup.\n\nTownspeople: We didn't have enough food, say the people. But we added our food together and now we all have tasty soup!":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9becb6eff3b9608eaa83.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b02e84fc90152273c431.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Hans"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/8f020076d8632b8fc3df.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Woman"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9338a70b304871ad3980.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1e8b58683f7072601c2e.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0339a5d6b24ef7b79c06.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5bae635012cb6baadf12.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0d98d6de52e3c413f48a.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Woman and her friend"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/535638c257f7f71e8ec5.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Hans"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/99c4422ee1aa3e2c1e1a.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Woman"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/2b49d204cd12cdb5bb57.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Woman's friend"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4205d7d83e77db4c10a9.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4d1afc9eba9a82e3a961.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Man and his son"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/af1ddb86f0654e6c8918.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/2ee6ebdddefbbe2e49dd.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a952cb99a88bd2a399c5.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Son"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/c4c0e8a3e962ef1c6ab8.mp3","turn":16,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b0a4d15d6768e81100c4.mp3","turn":17,"speaker":"Townspeople"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6105bcd8fd5ea45e9c1b.mp3","turn":18,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94a063d93890deb06ffd.mp3","turn":19,"speaker":"Townspeople"}],"Narrator: Tomas Flores is a farmer. He doesn't have a lot of money. He grows carrots, potatoes, and onions. He and his wife, Rosa, work hard every day. Farmer Flores has a cow. It gives lots of milk every day. Mrs. Flores sells the milk at the market in town. One day, Mrs. Flores comes home from town. She's very excited.\n\nMrs. Flores: There's a dance in town on Saturday. Can we go?\n\nFarmer Flores: I'm sorry, but no, says Farmer Flores. We're plain people. It's too fancy for us!\n\nNarrator: His wife is very sad. The next day, Farmer Flores has an idea. He takes the cow to town and sells it at the market. He buys a very fancy hat for himself and a beautiful dress for his wife. He runs home. He puts on the fancy hat. He gives his wife the beautiful dress.\n\nFarmer Flores: We can go to the dance, he says.\n\nNarrator: His wife is angry!\n\nMrs. Flores: Our cow gives us milk every day! she says. We sell the milk. We get money to buy food!\n\nFarmer Flores: But you want beautiful clothes for the dance, says Farmer Flores.\n\nMrs. Flores: Can we eat the fancy hat and the beautiful dress? Mrs. Flores asks.\n\nFarmer Flores: No, we can't, says the farmer. We need our cow!\n\nNarrator: Farmer Flores takes the dress and the hat back to the market. He buys his cow back.\n\nFarmer Flores: Now he tells people, Never sell something you need to buy something you want.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/bec1cfc7bc2a7f41b06f.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/19a486eae7d478cf8648.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Mrs. Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/2e69211aa26f4ee46bde.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Farmer Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a90074e53c9f19ab1fcc.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/cb4a86e90b774bb6d122.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Farmer Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/8ea1177971a3b4ea281f.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/55e7fd96a11439fd4ae7.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Mrs. Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/14fbfc0b91f4a90c86b7.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Farmer Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/417d43c16ea3958a9270.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Mrs. Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6e2e7dbef2d6c98570f4.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Farmer Flores"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/788d247e66cecdb47330.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6e815bbf5e52818ec20d.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Farmer Flores"}],"Narrator: City Mouse lives in the city.\n\nCity Mouse: There are too many people and cars here. I want some fresh air! I can visit my cousin, Country Mouse, he says.\n\nNarrator: City Mouse flies to the country. Country Mouse runs to him.\n\nCountry Mouse: Hello, City Mouse! Welcome to my home!\n\nCity Mouse: Thanks, Country Mouse! says City Mouse. I'm hungry. What's for dinner?\n\nNarrator: They go to the cornfield and eat some corn. Then they go to the orchard and eat some apples.\n\nCity Mouse: This food is okay, but it's too plain for me! says City Mouse.\n\nNarrator: It's bedtime and they're tired. They sleep in an old barn. The next morning, they walk to the pond.\n\nCity Mouse: The country is okay, but it's too boring for me, says City Mouse. Come with me to the city! It's interesting there.\n\nCountry Mouse: OK, says Country Mouse.\n\nNarrator: City Mouse and Country Mouse take a train to the city. They go to a movie theater, a department store, and a restaurant. They eat cheese and cookies.\n\nCountry Mouse: This food is okay, but it's too fancy for me, says Country Mouse.\n\nNarrator: It's bedtime and they're tired. They sleep in a new hotel. The next morning, they hear a loud noise.\n\nCity Mouse: Cats! Run! says City Mouse.\n\nNarrator: City Mouse and Country Mouse run and run until they are safe.\n\nCountry Mouse: The city is okay, but it's too dangerous for me! says Country Mouse. Come with me to the country. It's safe there.\n\nCity Mouse: No, the country is good for you, and the city is good for me, says City Mouse.\n\nNarrator: The two mice say goodbye and go home happy.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9e6740a1fea3a9048a9c.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/31feb80b39e70e216c84.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/341942eaf706a3b3f4ef.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/02b4ebc82e61ee17deac.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Country Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/02f7c4fb760e78db73eb.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e7672a7142f4263812bf.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/eac8a7d000a4dea35873.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b0667b79b4ed39cb0b58.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/15367f29698afcc3506d.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6fc8155676b1b949cb79.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Country Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a94ba6ac6219e20f5698.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9f9b5777092288501ac9.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Country Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/cd66f082b9ced82aaa0c.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/932fb37ff0c318a5ab02.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0fd98411d2524dbc51a6.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/c9db644b7dea4c94aff6.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Country Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/fd69ddff10b3fc3aa3dc.mp3","turn":16,"speaker":"City Mouse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6b7cec3be277fa815e94.mp3","turn":17,"speaker":"Narrator"}],"Maddie: January I'm Maddie and we're students in Ms. King's class. We want music lessons, but we don't have instruments. We can't buy instruments because we don't have any money. We have a big problem. We need a good idea. February We think, and think, and think, and then get an idea. Let's make instruments and give a concert! We can sell tickets, get money, and buy new instruments. But how do we make instruments? We ask our friends and families. Aha! We can use things from our homes. April We're making instruments that we can shake. We're using paper rolls and beads. Fay and Oscar are shaking them. Evan and Kate are using jars and candy. They're shaking them to a beat. May We're all practicing our instruments. These buckets and pots are our drums. Bruno, Sara, and Dan are striking them. These are our cymbals. Aziz and I are striking them together. Ms. King is helping us. What do you think? Are we having fun? June It's concert night. Look at all the people! They're buying tickets. Everyone is excited. We're all playing our instruments, singing, and dancing. Our parents are taking pictures. The people are clapping and giving money! It's a wonderful concert. September Look! These are our new instruments! We're very happy. We're playing them and we sound great. We still like our old instruments, too!":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9e86b851c475bd0834cb.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Maddie"}],"Narrator: One day, an old woman makes a gingerbread man cookie. She bakes it in the oven.\n\nOld woman: It smells good! I'm hungry!\n\nNarrator: The old woman opens the oven door. The gingerbread man jumps up and runs out the door!\n\nOld woman and old man: Stop! Don't run away! We want to eat you!\n\nNarrator: The old woman and old man chase the gingerbread man. He should run fast!\n\nGingerbread Man: Run, run as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the gingerbread man!\n\nNarrator: The gingerbread man sees a chicken in the yard.\n\nChicken: Stop! Don't run away! I want to eat you!\n\nNarrator: The old woman, old man, and the chicken all chase the gingerbread man. But he's too fast.\n\nGingerbread Man: Run, run as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the gingerbread man!\n\nNarrator: He sees a cow in a grassy field.\n\nCow: Stop! Don't run away! I want to eat you!\n\nNarrator: The old woman, old man, chicken, and the cow all chase the gingerbread man. But he's too fast.\n\nGingerbread Man: Run, run as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the gingerbread man!\n\nNarrator: He sees a horse next to a tree.\n\nHorse: Stop! Don't run away! I want to eat you!\n\nNarrator: The old woman, old man, chicken, cow, and the horse all chase the gingerbread man. But he's too fast.\n\nGingerbread Man: Run, run as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the gingerbread man!\n\nNarrator: The gingerbread man comes to a river. He should swim across it!\n\nGingerbread Man: Oh, no! I can't swim!\n\nNarrator: The gingerbread man sees a fox. He shouldn't talk to the fox!\n\nFox: You really shouldn't stay here. I can help you. Climb on my nose and we can cross the river.\n\nGingerbread Man: OK!\n\nNarrator: The gingerbread man jumps on the fox's nose. The fox throws the gingerbread man up in the air and ...\n\nFox: Yum! Delicious!\n\nNarrator: And that's the end of the gingerbread man!":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/55be99e71a5f441e8e0e.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/182a9d315e39765e04e3.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Old woman"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/90b657dc5da9cb19ac9f.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/058f543a467a0ec2bfda.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Old woman and old man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b7ae429629359ee8ce1a.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94e115e9af1f725af382.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6cc7ab13f77eb9fd24de.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/75da6360780c1ca45210.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Chicken"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9f77bc7881c141e60a12.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94e115e9af1f725af382.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/83ed341510465581edd3.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/75da6360780c1ca45210.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Cow"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94581b57f6e7200ef3b4.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94e115e9af1f725af382.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/7cc55b7a1a16f2032be8.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/75da6360780c1ca45210.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Horse"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/fa7e6246b698729f90f6.mp3","turn":16,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/94e115e9af1f725af382.mp3","turn":17,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/bc4d70396bc9f9237e56.mp3","turn":18,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0ec09fc39feaed161591.mp3","turn":19,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/29679a394443e257c3ad.mp3","turn":20,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/65efafd123f8a1afada5.mp3","turn":21,"speaker":"Fox"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1023414f726fb13d7de9.mp3","turn":22,"speaker":"Gingerbread Man"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/7ffae706a6e8fb6ed7db.mp3","turn":23,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/audio/gap-cue.wav","turn":23,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f9a4c448a430d2cfc38a.mp3","turn":24,"speaker":"Fox"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3f9755622aebf117da82.mp3","turn":25,"speaker":"Narrator"}]}}